course: dictionary
lesson: 13373
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the words around it. «The old house is haunted, so nobody lives there.» A house cannot be sad or tired, so haunted must mean that people believe ghosts visit it.
explain: «The memory of the storm haunted him for weeks.» A memory cannot visit a house, so this meaning is different. Haunted here means the memory kept coming back into his mind. Haunted is also the past form of the verb haunt, so it can describe something that keeps returning.
explain: «She had a haunted look after the bad news.» The clue is after the bad news, so her face looks worried or upset. Haunted here shows she seems troubled by something.
explain: Always test your meaning by putting it into the sentence. Haunt can also mean going often to a place, as in «He haunted the library every Saturday.» Read the whole sentence, then pick the meaning that fits.
fact: Haunted is an adjective, and it is also the past form of the verb haunt.
fact: «A haunted house» means a house that people believe ghosts visit.
fact: «Haunted by the memory» means a memory keeps coming back into your mind.
fact: «A haunted look» means a worried or upset look.
fact: «He haunted the library» means he went there often.
exercise: «The children dared each other to enter the haunted house at the end of the lane.» What does haunted mean here? | *Believed to be visited by ghosts | Painted bright red | Very clean and tidy | Very new and shiny
exercise: «The sound of the crash haunted her for years.» What does haunted mean here? | Laughed loudly | *Kept coming back to her mind | Went to visit a museum | Was ready to leave
exercise: «Mia had a haunted look on her face after the bad news.» What does haunted suggest? | *Worried or upset | Excited and happy | Cold and wet | Sleepy after lunch
test: «Tom haunted the playground every break, hoping to meet his friends.» What does haunted mean here? | *Went often to a place | Was afraid of the dark | Painted the fence | Believed to be visited by ghosts
test: «Her haunted expression showed she had not slept.» What does haunted mean? | Believed to be visited by ghosts | Painted a picture | Very cheerful | *Looking worried or upset
exam: «The memory of the lost puppy haunted Ella all night.» What does haunted mean? | Was found in the park | Looked very happy | *Kept coming back to her mind | Went to bed early
